"math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "61e0c9674e24eb63ece877fe2e32be869246f2c54dfc72c7c224b3b79bf5f6d6"} {"question" "q-12011" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "61e0c9674e24eb63ece877fe2e32be869246f2c54dfc72c7c224b3b79bf5f6d6"} {"question" "e-5431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5431.json" "file_sha256" "c606129d9da5ffb0b7d86efa8f5acf38ce7c71e5674f4d587ec68c2df22252dc"} {"question" "e-5431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n    Notice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5431.json" "file_sha256" "c606129d9da5ffb0b7d86efa8f5acf38ce7c71e5674f4d587ec68c2df22252dc"} {"question" "e-5433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is $[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5433.json" "file_sha256" "1d5f00300878dcf71bc5f594f5818b1b1c9dbd133a7d7357a8a277158e39b7be"} {"question" "e-5433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider a general vector $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5433.json" "file_sha256" "1d5f00300878dcf71bc5f594f5818b1b1c9dbd133a7d7357a8a277158e39b7be"} {"question" "e-5434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5434.json" "file_sha256" "03e3178afb3a62c4db1ea033e7435ac03875fc1f8025732ed8e3ff5419d6018b"} {"question" "e-5434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5434.json" "file_sha256" "03e3178afb3a62c4db1ea033e7435ac03875fc1f8025732ed8e3ff5419d6018b"} {"question" "e-5432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5432.json" "file_sha256" "ec9136f469b3b707a2daa92bf1e5b5d2d5751583a26641e1672b94166cbf9399"} {"question" "e-5432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5432.json" "file_sha256" "ec9136f469b3b707a2daa92bf1e5b5d2d5751583a26641e1672b94166cbf9399"}] "usage" {"e-5432" [] "q-37881" [] "e-5433" [] "e-5431" [] "e-5434" []} "basis" 853 "retractions" [[17592186125027 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T$, find $T(v)$.\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124239 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124239 :question/worked-solution "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\nNotice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124241 :question/problem "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is $\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124241 :question/worked-solution "Consider a general vector $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ Multiplying by the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}8x - y \\\\ -5x - 2y\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186124242 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$.\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124242 :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(v) &= T \\cdot v \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}27 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186124240 :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124240 :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNotice that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186123185 17592186123186 17592186123187 17592186123188 17592186123189] "immutable_fields" [[17592186123184 :answer-field/correct] [17592186123184 :answer-field/id] [17592186123184 :answer-field/key] [17592186123184 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
